
==============================================================================
SCENARIO 4 — Effect of Network Delay
==============================================================================

── Testing with network_delay_ms=0 on replica1's outgoing replication ────
[config] mode=eventual  delays: replica1=0ms, replica2=0ms, replica3=0ms
$ docker compose restart
time="2026-06-19T22:05:42+03:30" level=warning msg="/mnt/c/Users/sarag/Downloads/HW3/docker-compose.yml: the attribute `version` is obsolete, it will be ignored, please remove it to avoid potential confusion"
 Container replica1  Restarting
 Container replica2  Restarting
 Container replica3  Restarting
 Container replica2  Started
 Container replica1  Started
 Container replica3  Started

── Waiting for all replicas to become healthy ────────────────────────────
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8080/health'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:42] HEALTH replica1 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.8ms  body={"replica": "replica1", "status": "ok", "time": "2026-06-19T18:35:42Z"}
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8081/health'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:42] HEALTH replica2 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.8ms  body={"replica": "replica2", "status": "ok", "time": "2026-06-19T18:35:42Z"}
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8082/health'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:42] HEALTH replica3 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=2.2ms  body={"replica": "replica3", "status": "ok", "time": "2026-06-19T18:35:42Z"}

── PUT w_delay_0=A on replica1 ───────────────────────────────────────────
$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/put -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"key":"w_delay_0","value":"A"}'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:42] PUT(delay=0ms) replica1 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.8ms  body={"success": true, "replica_id": "", "data": {"key": "w_delay_0", "value": "A", "version": 1, "updated_by": "replica1", "updated_at": "2026-06-19T18:35:42.791778452Z"}, "latency_ms": 0.218}

── Polling replica2 for convergence (delay=0ms) ──────────────────────────
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8081/get?key=w_delay_0'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:42] GET(poll 1, delay=0ms) replica2 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.6ms  body={"success": true, "replica_id": "", "data": {"key": "w_delay_0", "value": "A", "version": 1, "updated_by": "replica1", "updated_at": "2026-06-19T18:35:42.791778452Z"}, "latency_ms": 0.043}

── Result for delay=0ms ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PUT latency: 1.8ms  (should stay flat regardless of delay, since eventual mode doesn't block on replication)
  Convergence time: 4.01ms  (should track closely with injected delay of 0ms)

